{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0a6f5d8b-f215-4810-ac75-4c3b48ff3b44","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb6a4b341ae686ba","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-ito67jrk/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E003.md","content":"# Workspace-aware artifacts-only serving in the MLflow tracking server\n\n## Description\n\nMake the MLflow tracking server's `--artifacts-only` mode composable with the\nexisting `--enable-workspaces` flag so that the artifacts-only server\nvalidates artifact requests against workspace (tenant) boundaries. When both\nflags are set, the server requires an explicit `--workspace-store-uri`,\ninitializes only the workspace provider needed to validate artifact requests,\nkeeps tracking and model registry stores uninitialized, and keeps\nnon-artifact API endpoints disabled. No new server flag is introduced — the\nworkspace-aware behavior emerges from combining existing flags.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Server flag composition: allow `--artifacts-only` to combine with\n  `--enable-workspaces`; when both are set, require an explicit\n  `--workspace-store-uri` (server fails to start with a clear error if it is\n  missing) and initialize only the workspace provider.\n- Keep tracking stores and model registry stores uninitialized and\n  non-artifact API endpoints disabled in the combined mode.\n- Workspace validation in artifact request handling: for each artifact\n  request, resolve the artifact path to its parent experiment (artifacts are\n  stored under experiment-scoped paths, e.g.\n  `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`), look up the experiment's workspace\n  assignment via the workspace store, and delegate authorization to the\n  existing auth plugin infrastructure. Requests failing workspace validation\n  receive HTTP 403.\n- Fail-closed behavior: when workspace-aware mode is active but the workspace\n  store is unreachable, artifact requests are denied (HTTP 503 indicating\n  workspace validation is unavailable), never served without validation.\n- Backwards compatibility: `--artifacts-only` without `--enable-workspaces`\n  retains current behavior (no workspace validation); deployments that do not\n  set `--enable-workspaces` are unaffected; no existing API contracts, CLI\n  arguments, or configuration keys change meaning.\n- Audit logging of workspace access denials in artifact serving through\n  server logs (denials emit a log record on the same denial code path).\n- If the split-server routing design requires a tracking-server-side\n  configuration change to delegate artifact operations to a dedicated\n  artifacts-only instance, implement that configuration change.\n- Document limitations of artifact path resolution for non-standard artifact\n  roots (initial implementation is scoped to the S3 artifact store, the\n  standard RHOAI configuration).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given the server started with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces\n  --workspace-store-uri kubernetes://` and a user who is a member of\n  workspace A, when the user requests an artifact belonging to an experiment\n  in workspace A, then the artifact is served — measured by HTTP 200 with\n  correct artifact content.\n- Given the same deployment and a user who is a member of workspace A but not\n  workspace B, when the user requests an artifact belonging to an experiment\n  in workspace B, then the request is denied — measured by HTTP 403 with an\n  error message indicating insufficient workspace permissions, and a\n  corresponding audit log record in the server logs.\n- Given the server started with `--artifacts-only` without\n  `--enable-workspaces`, when any authenticated user requests an artifact,\n  then it is served without workspace validation — measured by HTTP 200\n  regardless of workspace membership (current behavior preserved).\n- Given the workspace-aware artifacts-only server running and the workspace\n  store (Kubernetes API) unreachable, when a user requests an artifact, then\n  the request is denied — measured by HTTP 503 indicating workspace\n  validation is unavailable (fail-closed).\n- Given `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces` set without\n  `--workspace-store-uri`, the server fails to start with a clear error\n  message.\n- In the combined mode, tracking and model registry stores remain\n  uninitialized and non-artifact API endpoints remain disabled — measured by\n  server startup behavior and endpoint availability.\n- Regression: server behavior with either flag used individually (and with\n  neither) is unchanged from current behavior — measured by the existing\n  server test suite passing.\n- Limitations of artifact path resolution for non-standard artifact roots are\n  documented.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): `--artifacts-only` composable with `--enable-workspaces` and\n  `--workspace-store-uri` for workspace-validated artifact serving.\n- HLR-2 (P0): artifact requests validated against workspace membership;\n  non-members denied HTTP 403.\n- HLR-3 (P0): fail-closed when the workspace store is unreachable.\n- HLR-4 (P0): single-tenant / no-workspace-flag deployments retain current\n  behavior.\n- HLR-8 (P2, bundled): audit logging for workspace access denials through\n  server logs — emitted from the same artifact-request denial code path as\n  HLR-2/HLR-3; instrumented here rather than in a separate epic because a\n  split would touch the same handlers twice.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Artifact path resolution complexity: artifact paths may not map\n  straightforwardly to experiment IDs in all storage backends or custom\n  artifact root configurations. Mitigation: scope to the S3 artifact store\n  (standard RHOAI configuration) and document limitations for non-standard\n  artifact roots.\n- Performance: workspace resolution adds a workspace store lookup and auth\n  plugin validation per artifact request. No latency target is specified;\n  short-TTL caching of workspace membership decisions (consistent with\n  existing caching patterns in the tracking server's auth path) is a\n  deferrable follow-up pending the PM/Engineering latency decision.\n- Workspace validation delegates to the plugin's workspace resolution, which\n  must function in the artifacts-only context — the plugin workstream\n  provides that capability.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":56095,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a01dccb897beabeb","agent_id":"afb03082dd7d72f20","session_id":"994175ee-dc03-4507-860b-d2f574f96031","uuid":"b46055ba-db87-4870-a038-30917424c29a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:48:19.989Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
