{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0a6f5d8b-f215-4810-ac75-4c3b48ff3b44","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b91bcb911edd3c20","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-ito67jrk/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E004.md","content":"# mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context\n\n## Description\n\nVerify and, where needed, extend the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin\nso that workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only server\ncontext, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized.\nThe plugin already provides experiment-to-workspace mapping for the tracking\nserver's non-artifact operations (registered through the\n`mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by\n`WorkspaceStoreRegistry`); this epic makes that resolution available to the\nartifacts-only proxy. If the resolution is coupled to the full tracking\nserver initialization path, factor it into an independent initialization path\nwithin the plugin. The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name\nkubernetes-auth` authentication setup are unchanged.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Verify the plugin's workspace resolution operates in the artifacts-only\n  server context without tracking store or model registry store\n  initialization, per the feasibility investigation's findings.\n- If the investigation found coupling to the full server initialization path:\n  refactor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within\n  the plugin so it can be initialized with only the workspace provider.\n- Ensure workspace resolution from artifact request paths works through the\n  workspace store (`kubernetes://`) — resolving the parent experiment's\n  workspace assignment for authorization.\n- Preserve the plugin's existing behavior for the tracking server's\n  non-artifact operations (no regression in the full-server context).\n- Provide test coverage demonstrating workspace resolution with tracking and\n  model registry stores uninitialized.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Workspace resolution succeeds in the artifacts-only context with tracking\n  and model registry stores uninitialized — measured by a passing\n  test that initializes the plugin's workspace resolution standalone and\n  resolves an experiment's workspace assignment from an artifact request path\n  via the workspace store.\n- If refactoring was required: the independent initialization path is in\n  place and the plugin's resolution no longer requires tracking store or\n  model registry store initialization — measured by the same standalone\n  initialization test and by import/initialization dependency checks.\n- No regression in the tracking server's non-artifact workspace resolution —\n  measured by the plugin's existing test suite passing.\n- The plugin's authorization decision interface used by the artifacts-only\n  proxy is documented for the server workstream to build against.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 (P1): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the\n  artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization.\n- Supports HLR-2 (P0): the server's workspace validation delegates\n  authorization to this plugin infrastructure.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The strategy's risk register flags possible coupling of the plugin's\n  workspace resolution to the tracking server's full initialization path; the\n  feasibility investigation resolves this before implementation begins, and\n  this epic's scope (verification only vs. refactor) follows its outcome.\n- This epic inherits P0 priority: although HLR-7 is P1, the server-side P0\n  workspace validation builds against this plugin's resolution interface.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":56095,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a01dccb897beabeb","agent_id":"afb03082dd7d72f20","session_id":"994175ee-dc03-4507-860b-d2f574f96031","uuid":"5dea6fb2-7880-41b8-9fe5-3c59633963fd","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:48:29.181Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
