{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-90f4a020-da51-4a2b-abba-b69f3b3e8286","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c9b5832db7093d9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-ito67jrk/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E006.md","content":"# End-to-end integration validation of workspace-aware artifact serving\n\n## Description\n\nValidate workspace-aware artifact serving end to end through the\noperator-deployed split-server topology: multi-tenant workspace scenarios,\nbackwards compatibility and single-tenant regression, fail-closed edge cases,\nand split-server artifact traffic routing. This epic produces the automated\nintegration test suite and the validated evidence that the strategy's\nacceptance criteria hold when the server capability, the plugin workspace\nresolution, and the operator topology run together.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Automated end-to-end test suite covering the strategy's multi-tenant\n  scenarios against an operator-deployed split-server MLflow deployment:\n  workspace member access to own-workspace artifacts, cross-workspace denial,\n  behavior without workspace flags, and workspace store unavailability.\n- Split-server routing validation: artifact requests through the main\n  tracking deployment's entry point reach the dedicated artifacts-only\n  instance and are workspace-validated there.\n- Backwards compatibility and single-tenant regression scenarios:\n  deployments without `--enable-workspaces` and CRs without split-server\n  artifact serving retain current behavior.\n- Fail-closed edge cases: workspace store (Kubernetes API) unreachable during\n  artifact requests; recovery behavior when the store returns.\n- Misconfiguration scenarios: operator validation rejecting artifacts-only\n  configurations lacking workspace flags.\n- Execution of the suite against the built server image, plugin, and operator\n  to produce validated results.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a multi-tenant deployment where the artifacts-only instance runs with\n  `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes://`\n  and a user who is a member of workspace A, when the user requests an\n  artifact belonging to an experiment in workspace A through the deployed\n  topology, then the artifact is served — measured by HTTP 200 with correct\n  artifact content in the automated suite.\n- Given the same deployment and a user who is a member of workspace A but not\n  workspace B, when the user requests an artifact belonging to an experiment\n  in workspace B, then the request is denied — measured by HTTP 403 with an\n  insufficient-workspace-permissions error.\n- Given the workspace store unreachable, when a user requests an artifact\n  through the deployed topology, then the request is denied — measured by\n  HTTP 503 indicating workspace validation is unavailable (fail-closed).\n- Given a deployment without `--enable-workspaces` (or a CR without\n  split-server artifact serving), when any authenticated user requests an\n  artifact, then current behavior is retained — measured by HTTP 200\n  regardless of workspace membership and by topology parity with the\n  pre-change deployment.\n- Artifact requests entering through the main tracking deployment's entry\n  point are served by the dedicated artifacts-only instance — measured by\n  routing observability in the test scenario (e.g., request logs / tracing of\n  the artifacts-only instance).\n- The integration test suite is automated, reproducible from the repository,\n  and its executed run against the built components passes.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- End-to-end validation of HLR-1, HLR-2, HLR-3, HLR-4 (P0): the strategy's\n  acceptance criteria for workspace-validated, fail-closed, backwards\n  compatible artifact serving, measured through the deployed topology.\n- End-to-end validation of HLR-5, HLR-6 (P1): dedicated artifacts-only\n  Deployment/Service/HTTPRoute and artifact traffic routing to it.\n- HLR-7 (P1): plugin workspace resolution exercised in the artifacts-only\n  context as part of the end-to-end scenarios.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Requires the server capability, plugin workspace resolution, and operator\n  topology to be implemented; this epic is the acceptance gate that runs\n  them together.\n- Latency overhead of per-request workspace resolution is measured as an\n  observation during these scenarios, but no pass/fail latency threshold is\n  set pending the PM/Engineering decision on acceptable overhead.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":58324,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a01dccb897beabeb","agent_id":"afb03082dd7d72f20","session_id":"994175ee-dc03-4507-860b-d2f574f96031","uuid":"f69c0fce-dfb3-4440-919a-4120385dfbea","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:48:55.422Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
