{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e9bb17594d8c58c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n3\ttitle: mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the feasibility investigation finds workspace resolution is\n15\t    not coupled to tracking store initialization, this epic reduces to verification\n16\t    plus test coverage; if coupling is found, the refactor factors workspace resolution\n17\t    into an independent initialization path within the plugin per the investigation's\n18\t    refactoring plan.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 0\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 6\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tVerify and, where needed, extend the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin\n41\tso that workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only server\n42\tcontext, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized.\n43\tThe plugin already provides experiment-to-workspace mapping for the tracking\n44\tserver's non-artifact operations (registered through the\n45\t`mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by\n46\t`WorkspaceStoreRegistry`); this epic makes that resolution available to the\n47\tartifacts-only proxy. If the resolution is coupled to the full tracking\n48\tserver initialization path, factor it into an independent initialization path\n49\twithin the plugin. The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name\n50\tkubernetes-auth` authentication setup are unchanged.\n51\t\n52\t## Scope\n53\t\n54\t- Verify the plugin's workspace resolution operates in the artifacts-only\n55\t  server context without tracking store or model registry store\n56\t  initialization, per the feasibility investigation's findings.\n57\t- If the investigation found coupling to the full server initialization path:\n58\t  refactor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within\n59\t  the plugin so it can be initialized with only the workspace provider.\n60\t- Ensure workspace resolution from artifact request paths works through the\n61\t  workspace store (`kubernetes://`) — resolving the parent experiment's\n62\t  workspace assignment for authorization.\n63\t- Preserve the plugin's existing behavior for the tracking server's\n64\t  non-artifact operations (no regression in the full-server context).\n65\t- Provide test coverage demonstrating workspace resolution with tracking and\n66\t  model registry stores uninitialized.\n67\t\n68\t## Acceptance Criteria\n69\t\n70\t- Workspace resolution succeeds in the artifacts-only context with tracking\n71\t  and model registry stores uninitialized — measured by a passing\n72\t  test that initializes the plugin's workspace resolution standalone and\n73\t  resolves an experiment's workspace assignment from an artifact request path\n74\t  via the workspace store.\n75\t- If refactoring was required: the independent initialization path is in\n76\t  place and the plugin's resolution no longer requires tracking store or\n77\t  model registry store initialization — measured by the same standalone\n78\t  initialization test and by import/initialization dependency checks.\n79\t- No regression in the tracking server's non-artifact workspace resolution —\n80\t  measured by the plugin's existing test suite passing.\n81\t- The plugin's authorization decision interface used by the artifacts-only\n82\t  proxy is documented for the server workstream to build against.\n83\t\n84\t## HLR Traceability\n85\t\n86\t- HLR-7 (P1): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the\n87\t  artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization.\n88\t- Supports HLR-2 (P0): the server's workspace validation delegates\n89\t  authorization to this plugin infrastructure.\n90\t\n91\t## Risks / Notes\n92\t\n93\t- The strategy's risk register flags possible coupling of the plugin's\n94\t  workspace resolution to the tracking server's full initialization path; the\n95\t  feasibility investigation resolves this before implementation begins, and\n96\t  this epic's scope (verification only vs. refactor) follows its outcome.\n97\t- This epic inherits P0 priority: although HLR-7 is P1, the server-side P0\n98\t  workspace validation builds against this plugin's resolution interface.\n99\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b37286de055eda33","agent_id":"a6067bd9e01700627","session_id":"994175ee-dc03-4507-860b-d2f574f96031","uuid":"ed891404-b273-4376-802c-265ff9183f1f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:52:21.771Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e9bb17594d8c58c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
