{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d05f39d3b021590","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n3\ttitle: MLflow operator split-server topology for the artifacts-only instance\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the routing design investigation determines the tracking server\n15\t    needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations, the routing scope\n16\t    of this epic is rewritten to the adopted design (and the server-side delegation\n17\t    change lands in the server workstream); if HTTPRoute-level routing suffices, routing\n18\t    is implemented purely via Gateway API resources.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 0\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 6\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# MLflow operator split-server topology for the artifacts-only instance\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tExtend the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow\n41\tinstance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute, forming\n42\ta split-server topology: the main tracking deployment handles experiment\n43\ttracking, model registry, and prompt registry, while the artifacts-only\n44\tinstance handles artifact serving with workspace validation. The operator\n45\tadditionally configures the main tracking deployment to route artifact\n46\ttraffic to the dedicated instance, per the routing design. This is a\n47\tsplit-server topology, not a single-deployment configuration toggle.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- New Helm chart templates for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and\n52\t  HTTPRoute, rendered through the operator's existing Helm-in-operator\n53\t  pattern (MLflow CR spec converted to Helm values, rendered through\n54\t  embedded chart templates, applied via Server-Side Apply).\n55\t- Propagate workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`,\n56\t  `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only\n57\t  instance using the same configuration mechanisms already used for the main\n58\t  tracking deployment, together with `--artifacts-only` and\n59\t  `--serve-artifacts`.\n60\t- Configure the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to the\n61\t  dedicated artifacts-only instance, per the routing design (HTTPRoute-level\n62\t  routing and/or tracking server delegation configuration, as the design\n63\t  investigation determined).\n64\t- Create Gateway API HTTPRoute resources for the artifacts-only instance\n65\t  conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the\n66\t  operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n67\t- Deploy the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar on the artifacts-only instance\n68\t  identically to the main tracking deployment (authentication layer\n69\t  unchanged).\n70\t- Operator validation: reject MLflow CR configurations where the\n71\t  artifacts-only instance is enabled but lacks the workspace flags, so that\n72\t  misconfiguration cannot result in artifact requests bypassing workspace\n73\t  validation.\n74\t- Backwards compatibility: MLflow CRs that do not enable split-server\n75\t  artifact serving reconcile to the current single-deployment topology\n76\t  unchanged.\n77\t\n78\t## Acceptance Criteria\n79\t\n80\t- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, when the\n81\t  operator reconciles the CR, then a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment,\n82\t  Service, and HTTPRoute are created separate from the main tracking\n83\t  Deployment — measured by the presence of distinct rendered resources with\n84\t  the correct flag combinations.\n85\t- The artifacts-only Deployment's container command runs with\n86\t  `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes://\n87\t  --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts` — measured by inspecting the\n88\t  container command in the rendered Deployment spec.\n89\t- The main tracking deployment is configured to route artifact traffic to\n90\t  the dedicated artifacts-only instance per the adopted routing design —\n91\t  measured by the rendered routing configuration and HTTPRoute resources.\n92\t- HTTPRoute resources for the artifacts-only instance are created only when\n93\t  the Gateway API CRDs are present at runtime — measured by reconcile\n94\t  behavior with and without the CRDs (conditional discovery pattern).\n95\t- An MLflow CR enabling the artifacts-only instance without workspace flags\n96\t  is rejected with a clear validation error — measured by reconcile status /\n97\t  event output.\n98\t- MLflow CRs without split-server artifact serving reconcile to the current\n99\t  topology unchanged — measured by rendered-resource parity with the\n100\t  pre-change output (rollback / opt-in safety).\n101\t\n102\t## HLR Traceability\n103\t\n104\t- HLR-5 (P1): operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a\n105\t  separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute.\n106\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the\n107\t  dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n108\t- HLR-4 (P0, backwards-compatibility aspect): the split topology is opt-in;\n109\t  CRs without it retain current behavior.\n110\t\n111\t## Risks / Notes\n112\t\n113\t- Split-deployment operational complexity: two Deployments, two Services,\n114\t  two HTTPRoutes, and artifact traffic routing add operational surface;\n115\t  misconfiguration could let artifact requests bypass workspace validation.\n116\t  Mitigation in scope: declarative single-CR management plus reconcile-time\n117\t  validation rejecting artifacts-only configurations that lack workspace\n118\t  flags.\n119\t- The rendered-resource acceptance criteria are verifiable without the new\n120\t  server capability; end-to-end behavior of the deployed topology is\n121\t  validated by the integration validation workstream.\n122\t- This epic exceeds the ~2-week guideline (2-3 sprints by the strategy's\n123\t  effort arithmetic). Kept whole because the split topology is one logical\n124\t  operator change — a single reconciliation path rendering one coordinated\n125\t  set of resources. Re-split trigger: the routing design lands on an\n126\t  approach requiring substantive server-side delegation changes in addition\n127\t  to the operator topology, at which point split into topology-provisioning\n128\t  and traffic-routing epics.\n129\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b37286de055eda33","agent_id":"a6067bd9e01700627","session_id":"994175ee-dc03-4507-860b-d2f574f96031","uuid":"89ea045c-2992-437b-82eb-912bb32d3d63","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:52:24.104Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d05f39d3b021590","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
