{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ff256f7e7e489fe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n3\ttitle: Workspace resolution feasibility in the artifacts-only server context\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: High\n19\tai_implementability_score: 3\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Workspace resolution feasibility in the artifacts-only server context\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the two gating unknowns that determine how\n30\tworkspace-aware artifact serving can be built: (1) whether artifact request\n31\tpaths carry enough information (experiment ID or run ID) to resolve workspace\n32\tmembership, and (2) whether workspace resolution in the\n33\t`mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin and the `kubernetes://` workspace store\n34\tdepends on tracking store or model registry store initialization. The outcome\n35\tdetermines the scope of both the server-side workspace validation work and the\n36\tplugin verification/refactoring work.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Trace the `/api/2.0/mlflow/artifacts/*` request paths in the MLflow server\n41\t  to determine whether they include sufficient information (experiment ID or\n42\t  run ID) to resolve the parent experiment and, via the workspace store, its\n43\t  workspace assignment — scoped to the standard RHOAI S3 artifact store\n44\t  configuration where artifact paths follow the\n45\t  `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` structure.\n46\t- Map the initialization dependency graph of the workspace resolution path in\n47\t  `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` (the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point\n48\t  loaded via `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`) to determine whether workspace\n49\t  resolution is coupled to the tracking server's full initialization path\n50\t  (tracking store, model registry store).\n51\t- Determine whether the `kubernetes://` workspace store provides\n52\t  experiment-to-workspace mapping that is accessible without initializing\n53\t  tracking stores.\n54\t- If coupling is found, produce a refactoring plan that factors workspace\n55\t  resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin, with a\n56\t  scope estimate.\n57\t- Verify the assumption that `--artifacts-only` and `--enable-workspaces` can\n58\t  be made composable without breaking the server initialization sequence for\n59\t  either flag used individually.\n60\t- Exercise the resolution path locally (the MLflow server and plugin are\n61\t  pip-installable; the Kubernetes API surface may be stubbed) to confirm the\n62\t  code-level findings.\n63\t\n64\t## Acceptance Criteria\n65\t\n66\t- A written determination, with code references and/or a reproducible local\n67\t  exercise, of whether artifact request paths in the\n68\t  `/api/2.0/mlflow/artifacts/*` endpoints carry sufficient information to\n69\t  resolve workspace membership under the S3 artifact store configuration,\n70\t  including any limitations for non-standard artifact roots.\n71\t- A written determination, with an explicit dependency graph, of whether\n72\t  plugin workspace store initialization depends on tracking store or model\n73\t  registry store availability.\n74\t- If coupling exists: a refactoring plan for an independent workspace\n75\t  resolution initialization path within the plugin, with scope estimate; if no\n76\t  coupling exists: a recorded verification that resolution works with stores\n77\t  uninitialized.\n78\t- A recorded recommendation on the composition of `--artifacts-only` with\n79\t  `--enable-workspaces` that either confirms the assumed initialization\n80\t  sequence or states what must change.\n81\t\n82\t## HLR Traceability\n83\t\n84\t- Prerequisite for HLR-1, HLR-2, HLR-3, HLR-7: the answers determine whether\n85\t  and how the server-side workspace validation (HLR-1/2/3) and the plugin\n86\t  workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context (HLR-7) can be built, and\n87\t  whether the plugin work is verification-only or requires refactoring.\n88\t\n89\t## Risks / Notes\n90\t\n91\t- The strategy flags both questions as open questions and\n92\t  validation-requiring assumptions; the strategy's own risk mitigation directs\n93\t  validating the plugin's initialization dependencies early, which this\n94\t  investigation does.\n95\t- Initial scope is the S3 artifact store (standard RHOAI configuration);\n96\t  non-standard artifact roots are documented as limitations, not supported.\n97\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae698ca7dc970245","agent_id":"a0ba675e7468d39d5","session_id":"994175ee-dc03-4507-860b-d2f574f96031","uuid":"565368cc-4455-4eac-97a4-c8f75d332149","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:57:24.555Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ff256f7e7e489fe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
