:\n\n- **E001 outcome A** (resolution feasible, plugin not coupled): E004 reduces to\n  verification plus tests. **Outcome B** (coupled): E004 additionally factors\n  workspace resolution into an independent initialization path — `rewrite`.\n- **E002 outcome A** (Gateway-level path routing suffices): E005 implements\n  routing purely via HTTPRoute resources; no server-side change exists.\n  **Outcome B** (tracking server needs a delegation configuration change):\n  the operator's routing scope is rewritten accordingly — `rewrite` — and the\n  server-side delegation configuration is owned by the conditional branch\n  epic **RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-B-E007** (gated on this outcome; `remove` if\n  outcome A holds). The main-plan server epic (workspace-aware\n  artifacts-only serving) is deliberately not blocked on the routing design:\n  its P0 scope (flag composition, workspace validation, fail-closed,\n  backwards compatibility) is independent of the topology decision, and the\n  delegation configuration serves only the P1 topology HLRs — so gating it\n  on the routing investigation would serialize P0 delivery behind P1\n  topology work and force the routing investigation to inherit P0.\n\n### Conditional branch epic (E002 outcome B)\n\nOne branch file exists, selected only when the routing design investigation\ndetermines the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate\nartifact operations:\n\n- **RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-B-E007** — Tracking server artifact-delegation\n  configuration for the split-server topology (Implementation, MLflow Team,\n  P1, component MLflow). Gated by the routing design investigation\n  (`gated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002`, `branch: B`,\n  `gate_failure_impact.action: remove`): under outcome A (HTTPRoute-level\n  routing suffices) the work item does not exist.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E002[RHAISTRAT-8009-E002 Routing design] --> B007[RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-B-E007 Server delegation config]\n```\n\nBranch epics are excluded from the main-plan DAG and critical path above,\nand a main-plan epic never lists one in its dependencies. `epic_count`\ncounts the six main-plan epics."}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":58118,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae698ca7dc970245","agent_id":"a0ba675e7468d39d5","session_id":"994175ee-dc03-4507-860b-d2f574f96031","uuid":"74e5ce3b-43d3-4aac-a4cb-4288ef594ab5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:02:24.326Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
