{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87cc3791f48b62f0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n3\ttitle: Artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves how the MLflow operator should configure artifact\n30\ttraffic routing from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated\n31\tartifacts-only instance in the split-server topology. The answer determines\n32\tthe HTTPRoute design and whether the tracking server itself needs a\n33\tconfiguration change to delegate artifact operations, and therefore shapes the\n34\tscope of both the operator topology work and any server-side delegation\n35\tconfiguration.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Determine how the main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the\n40\t  dedicated artifacts-only instance: whether Gateway API HTTPRoute-level path\n41\t  routing suffices, or whether the tracking server needs a configuration\n42\t  change to delegate artifact operations to another instance.\n43\t- Design the HTTPRoute resources for the artifacts-only instance's ingress,\n44\t  consistent with the operator's existing pattern of conditional HTTPRoute\n45\t  creation via runtime CRD discovery.\n46\t- Evaluate how the routing design interacts with the split-server topology\n47\t  (two Deployments, two Services, two HTTPRoutes) and with the operator's\n48\t  Helm-in-operator rendering (MLflow CR spec converted to Helm values,\n49\t  rendered through embedded chart templates, applied via Server-Side Apply).\n50\t- If the outcome requires a tracking-server-side configuration change,\n51\t  specify the scope of that change so it can be taken up as the\n52\t  conditional server-workstream branch work item selected by this\n53\t  outcome.\n54\t- Confirm the assumption that the operator's Helm chart rendering supports\n55\t  the addition of a second Deployment resource for the artifacts-only\n56\t  instance without structural changes to the chart architecture, or record\n57\t  what structural changes are needed.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- A documented routing design decision covering: the routing mechanism\n62\t  (HTTPRoute path routing and/or tracking server delegation configuration),\n63\t  the HTTPRoute resource design for the artifacts-only instance, and the\n64\t  configuration the main tracking deployment receives.\n65\t- An explicit determination of whether the tracking server needs a\n66\t  configuration change to delegate artifact operations, and if so, a\n67\t  specification of that change's scope.\n68\t- A determination of whether the existing Helm chart architecture supports the\n69\t  second Deployment without structural changes, with evidence from the chart\n70\t  templates.\n71\t- The design is validated against the operator's existing conditional CRD\n72\t  discovery pattern for optional dependencies (Gateway API HTTPRoutes created\n73\t  only when the CRDs are present).\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- Prerequisite for HLR-5 and HLR-6: the routing design determines how the\n78\t  operator deploys the dedicated artifacts-only instance's ingress (HLR-5)\n79\t  and how the main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to it (HLR-6).\n80\t\n81\t## Risks / Notes\n82\t\n83\t- Misconfiguration of artifact traffic routing could result in artifact\n84\t  requests bypassing workspace validation (strategy risk). The design must\n85\t  make the routed path enforce workspace validation; the operator workstream\n86\t  additionally validates configurations at reconcile time.\n87\t- The strategy lists this as an open question owned by the MLflow Team — a\n88\t  technical design decision, not a stakeholder decision.\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4ec5560b1a4b7b6","agent_id":"abc26509b17a1d42b","session_id":"994175ee-dc03-4507-860b-d2f574f96031","uuid":"db44188e-bf9a-4e1a-aaa5-8640b0ee46eb","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:03:55.255Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-87cc3791f48b62f0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
