{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6a877a687076a99","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n3\ttitle: MLflow operator split-server topology for the artifacts-only instance\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the routing design investigation determines the tracking server\n15\t    needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations, the routing scope\n16\t    of this epic is rewritten to the adopted design (and the server-side delegation\n17\t    change is owned by the conditional server-workstream branch work item selected\n18\t    by that outcome); if HTTPRoute-level routing suffices, routing is implemented\n19\t    purely via Gateway API resources.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 0\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: 0\n26\t  external_dependency: 1\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 6\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\tbranch: null\n36\t---\n37\t# MLflow operator split-server topology for the artifacts-only instance\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tExtend the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow\n42\tinstance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute, forming\n43\ta split-server topology: the main tracking deployment handles experiment\n44\ttracking, model registry, and prompt registry, while the artifacts-only\n45\tinstance handles artifact serving with workspace validation. The operator\n46\tadditionally configures the main tracking deployment to route artifact\n47\ttraffic to the dedicated instance, per the routing design. This is a\n48\tsplit-server topology, not a single-deployment configuration toggle.\n49\t\n50\t## Scope\n51\t\n52\t- New Helm chart templates for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and\n53\t  HTTPRoute, rendered through the operator's existing Helm-in-operator\n54\t  pattern (MLflow CR spec converted to Helm values, rendered through\n55\t  embedded chart templates, applied via Server-Side Apply).\n56\t- Propagate workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`,\n57\t  `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only\n58\t  instance using the same configuration mechanisms already used for the main\n59\t  tracking deployment, together with `--artifacts-only` and\n60\t  `--serve-artifacts`.\n61\t- Configure the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to the\n62\t  dedicated artifacts-only instance, per the routing design (HTTPRoute-level\n63\t  routing and/or tracking server delegation configuration, as the design\n64\t  investigation determined).\n65\t- Create Gateway API HTTPRoute resources for the artifacts-only instance\n66\t  conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the\n67\t  operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n68\t- Deploy the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar on the artifacts-only instance\n69\t  identically to the main tracking deployment (authentication layer\n70\t  unchanged).\n71\t- Operator validation: reject MLflow CR configurations where the\n72\t  artifacts-only instance is enabled but lacks the workspace flags, so that\n73\t  misconfiguration cannot result in artifact requests bypassing workspace\n74\t  validation.\n75\t- Backwards compatibility: MLflow CRs that do not enable split-server\n76\t  artifact serving reconcile to the current single-deployment topology\n77\t  unchanged.\n78\t\n79\t## Acceptance Criteria\n80\t\n81\t- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, when the\n82\t  operator reconciles the CR, then a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment,\n83\t  Service, and HTTPRoute are created separate from the main tracking\n84\t  Deployment — measured by the presence of distinct rendered resources with\n85\t  the correct flag combinations.\n86\t- The artifacts-only Deployment's container command runs with\n87\t  `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes://\n88\t  --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts` — measured by inspecting the\n89\t  container command in the rendered Deployment spec.\n90\t- The main tracking deployment is configured to route artifact traffic to\n91\t  the dedicated artifacts-only instance per the adopted routing design —\n92\t  measured by the rendered routing configuration and HTTPRoute resources.\n93\t- HTTPRoute resources for the artifacts-only instance are created only when\n94\t  the Gateway API CRDs are present at runtime — measured by reconcile\n95\t  behavior with and without the CRDs (conditional discovery pattern).\n96\t- An MLflow CR enabling the artifacts-only instance without workspace flags\n97\t  is rejected with a clear validation error — measured by reconcile status /\n98\t  event output.\n99\t- MLflow CRs without split-server artifact serving reconcile to the current\n100\t  topology unchanged — measured by rendered-resource parity with the\n101\t  pre-change output (rollback / opt-in safety).\n102\t\n103\t## HLR Traceability\n104\t\n105\t- HLR-5 (P1): operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a\n106\t  separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute.\n107\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the\n108\t  dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n109\t- HLR-4 (P0, backwards-compatibility aspect): the split topology is opt-in;\n110\t  CRs without it retain current behavior.\n111\t\n112\t## Risks / Notes\n113\t\n114\t- Split-deployment operational complexity: two Deployments, two Services,\n115\t  two HTTPRoutes, and artifact traffic routing add operational surface;\n116\t  misconfiguration could let artifact requests bypass workspace validation.\n117\t  Mitigation in scope: declarative single-CR management plus reconcile-time\n118\t  validation rejecting artifacts-only configurations that lack workspace\n119\t  flags.\n120\t- The rendered-resource acceptance criteria are verifiable without the new\n121\t  server capability; end-to-end behavior of the deployed topology is\n122\t  validated by the integration validation workstream.\n123\t- This epic exceeds the ~2-week guideline (2-3 sprints by the strategy's\n124\t  effort arithmetic). Kept whole because the split topology is one logical\n125\t  operator change — a single reconciliation path rendering one coordinated\n126\t  set of resources. Re-split trigger: the routing design lands on an\n127\t  approach requiring substantive server-side delegation changes in addition\n128\t  to the operator topology, at which point split into topology-provisioning\n129\t  and traffic-routing epics.\n130\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4ec5560b1a4b7b6","agent_id":"abc26509b17a1d42b","session_id":"994175ee-dc03-4507-860b-d2f574f96031","uuid":"4ad61908-e656-4623-84fc-4936bb379f21","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:03:57.234Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6a877a687076a99","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
